      "math_academy_id": "e-12949",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the orthogonal matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14160400/assets/6553a5d1c0005141d9c48a2c56c7b6372557ff0a7b876dad17ea9aea91a2196e.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nTherefore, since $D$ is orthogonal, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{-1} & ={D}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
